{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-16556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $7-6\\text{i}=(4p-3q\\text{i})(1+2\\text{i})$, calculate $p$ and $q.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-16556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we divide both sides of the equation by $1+2\\text{i}$ to isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7-6\\text{i} & =(4p-3q\\text{i})(1+2\\text{i}) \\\\ \\frac{7-6\\text{i}}{1+2\\text{i}} & =4p-3q\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(7-6\\text{i})(1-2\\text{i})}{(1+2\\text{i})(1-2\\text{i})} & =4p-3q\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{7-14\\text{i}-6\\text{i}+12{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{1}^{2}-(2\\text{i})^{2}} & =4p-3q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{-5-20\\text{i}}{1+4} & =4p-3q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{-5-20\\text{i}}{5} & =4p-3q\\text{i} \\\\ -1-4\\text{i} & =4p-3q\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $-1=4p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $-4=-3q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=-\\frac{1}{4}$ and $q=\\frac{4}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-16556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "898c51a332a85c43dfeb7ea2ad3e868a6bcd905a34005c83c3039413f583e610"} {"question" "q-16556" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-16556" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$p=-1$, $q=4$"] ["text" "$p=-4$, $q=3$"] ["text" "$p=-\\frac{1}{4}$, $q=\\frac{4}{3}$"] ["text" "$p=-\\frac{3}{4}$, $q=\\frac{5}{3}$"] ["text" "$p=\\frac{1}{4}$, $q=-\\frac{4}{3}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-16556" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$p=-\\frac{1}{4}$, $q=\\frac{4}{3}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-160037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $3+5\\text{i}=\\frac{p+\\text{i}q}{1-\\text{i}},$ calculate $p$ and $q.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-160037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $1-\\text{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3+5\\text{i} & =\\frac{p+\\text{i}q}{1-\\text{i}} \\\\ (3+5\\text{i})(1-\\text{i}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 3-3\\text{i}+5\\text{i}-5{\\text{i}}^{2} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 3+5+2\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 8+2\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n8=p.\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=8$ and $q=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-160037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "898c51a332a85c43dfeb7ea2ad3e868a6bcd905a34005c83c3039413f583e610"} {"question" "q-160037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-160037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$p=-3$, $q=2$"] ["text" "$p=-4$, $q=2$"] ["text" "$p=2$, $q=1$"] ["text" "$p=2$, $q=3$"] ["text" "$p=8$, $q=2$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-160037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$p=8$, $q=2$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-160046" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $8\\text{i}=(p+\\text{i}q)(2+2\\text{i})$, calculate $p$ and $q.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-160046" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we divide both sides of the equation by $2+2\\text{i}$ to isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\text{i} & =(p+\\text{i}q)(2+2\\text{i}) \\\\ \\frac{8\\text{i}}{2+2\\text{i}} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8\\text{i}(2-2\\text{i})}{(2+2\\text{i})(2-2\\text{i})} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{16\\text{i}-16{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{2}^{2}-(2\\text{i})^{2}} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{16+16\\text{i}}{8} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 2+2\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $2=p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $2=q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=2$ and $q=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-160046" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "898c51a332a85c43dfeb7ea2ad3e868a6bcd905a34005c83c3039413f583e610"} {"question" "q-160046" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-160046" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "p=-2,q=-2."] ["math" "p=-2,q=2."] ["math" "p=2,q=-2."] ["math" "p=2,q=2."] ["math" "p=\\frac{1}{2},q=-\\frac{1}{2}."]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-160046" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "p=2,q=2."] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-280441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If  $-3+2\\text{i}=\\frac{p+q\\text{i}}{1-4\\text{i}},$ then$\\,p=$\n{{field-1}}\nand\n$q=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-280441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $1-4\\text{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3+2\\text{i}=\\frac{p+q\\text{i}}{1-4\\text{i}} \\\\ (-3+2\\text{i})(1-4\\text{i}) & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ -3+12\\text{i}+2\\text{i}-8{\\text{i}}^{2} & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ -3+8+14\\text{i} & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ 5+14\\text{i} & =p+q\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n5=p.\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14 & =q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=5$ and $q=14.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-280441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "898c51a332a85c43dfeb7ea2ad3e868a6bcd905a34005c83c3039413f583e610"} {"question" "q-280441" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-280441" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-280441" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-280441" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-281168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If  $\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}-\\text{i}}=p+\\text{i}q,$ then$\\,p=$\n{{field-1}}\nand\n$q=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-281168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}-\\text{i}} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{5(\\sqrt{2}+\\text{i})}{(\\sqrt{2}-\\text{i})(\\sqrt{2}+\\text{i})} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{5(\\sqrt{2}+\\text{i})}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}-(\\text{i})^{2}} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{5(\\sqrt{2}+\\text{i})}{2+1} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{5(\\sqrt{2}+\\text{i})}{3} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{3}+\\frac{5}{3}\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{3}=p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $\\frac{5}{3}=q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{3}$ and $q=\\frac{5}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-281168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "898c51a332a85c43dfeb7ea2ad3e868a6bcd905a34005c83c3039413f583e610"} {"question" "q-281168" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579/state.json" "file_sha256" "022eff8eb3fe4929fa80a9e18bbf016bc12782a6ef84a2077927baa5e47a7deb"} {"question" "q-281168" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\sqrt{